KNOWNBUG
assignment-to-non-constant-index1.sv
--bound 2
^\[main\.p0\] always \(##1 \$past\(main\.we\) -> main\.mem\[\$past\(main\.addr\)\] == \$past\(main\.d\)\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The RTL construction rewrites an assignment to an array element with
a non-constant index into a with-expression on the whole array, using
the Verilog index as is. The internal representation stores the
element with the left index of the declared range in the first
position, and hence the index of an array with a decreasing range
must be mirrored, as done when lowering reads. The write and the read
of mem[addr] therefore disagree on the element.
